@startuml Statistics Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox
title Statistics — filtered database aggregation

actor Admin
participant StatisticsController as Controller
participant StatisticsService as Service
participant "Period + Filter services" as Filters
database "MySQL\nStatistics repositories" as Repository

Admin -> Controller : GET /statistics/{report}
Controller -> Service : validated report query
Service -> Filters : normalize date, academic period and grouping
Filters --> Service : effective filters
Service -> Repository : execute report-specific aggregate queries
Repository --> Service : counts, groups and time series
Service -> Service : calculate documented rates and rankings
Service --> Admin : explicit statistics DTO

note over Filters, Repository
  Aggregation stays in SQL, uses scoped boundaries and avoids duplicate joins.
  Empty data is returned as an explicit empty/zero report state.
end note
@enduml
